  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「オオバギ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%AA%E3%82%AA%E3%83%90%E3%82%AE",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 106351517,
      "text": "オオバギ は、トウダイグサ科の樹木の一種である。丸い大きな葉をつける。成長が早い先駆植物の樹木として知られる。別名オオバキ。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Macaranga tanarius」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macaranga_tanarius",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1372541460,
      "text": "Macaranga tanarius is a species of flowering plant found in South East Asia, Thailand, Papua New Guinea, South China, Taiwan, and eastern Australia. It is commonly seen as a pioneer species in disturbed rainforest areas. It is easily recognised for its round veiny leaves. In Australia, it naturally occurs from the Richmond River, New South Wales to Cooktown in tropical Queensland."
    }
